  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.639 acc / 0.620 F1. Adding image (resnet50) to the validated RNA pipeline (config_002, 0.591) yielded a meaningful ~5-point gain, confirming the image modality contributes. However, the image encoder dimension is entirely unexplored beyond resnet50. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l (a substantially larger, higher-capacity pretrained ViT) further improve multimodal performance, or is resnet50 already near the ceiling for the image contribution? Why this is the best next experiment: config_025 changes only the image encoder while holding every other parameter at its empirically validated best setting (multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion, pca_n2000). This isolates the image-encoder effect cleanly. If it improves, it identifies a clear exploitation path; if it does not, it confirms resnet50 is sufficient and redirects attention to the RNA encoder dimension. This is a high-information, low-risk extension of the current best configuration under a tight budget."
}

